{"guide":{"questionsToConsider":["What counts as critical for your service, and does the wording of the severity options match your incident policy?","Is there an urgent channel, like an on-call phone line, that people should use instead of the form for outages?","Which systems do people most often report? A dropdown of them may beat a free-text answer.","Who reads new reports, and during which hours?"],"howToUseResponses":"Triage from the severity and who-is-affected answers first, then assign an owner. Critical reports carry a phone number, so ring back rather than replying by email. Keep the start time and the resolution answer for the incident timeline, and export the reports to CSV each month to see which services break most and whether the same impact keeps coming up.","customizeSteps":["Rename the severity levels to match your incident process, keeping the critical option first so it routes to the callback question.","Replace the impact options with the parts of your product people depend on most.","Share the link in your help desk, status page and internal chat so reports land in one place, and review them in the dashboard."],"faqs":[{"q":"What should a software incident report include?","a":"The affected service, when it started, how severe it is, who is affected, what the person saw and what has been tried. A screenshot or error message makes it much faster to diagnose."},{"q":"Is an incident report the same as a bug report?","a":"Not quite. An incident report records a disruption to a running service, while a bug report describes a defect that may never have caused an outage."},{"q":"How do I handle critical incidents reported through a form?","a":"Make sure someone is watching for them. This form asks critical reporters for a phone number so the on-call engineer can call straight back."},{"q":"Can non-technical staff use this form?","a":"Yes. The questions are in plain language, and in the chat an AI follow-up asks for more detail when a description is too vague to act on."}]},"doc":{"schemaVersion":10,"title":"Software incident report","description":"Record what broke, when, how badly and for whom, in a shape your on-call team can triage.","blocks":[{"id":"blk_software00","ref":"welcome","title":"Something not working? Tell us what you're seeing and we'll get the right person on it.","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"buttonLabel":"Start","type":"welcome"},{"id":"blk_software01","ref":"reporter","title":"Who is reporting this?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"contact_info","fields":["first_name","last_name","email"]},{"id":"blk_software02","ref":"service","title":"Which system, app or service is affected?","description":"As specific as you can, for example the billing page in the customer portal.","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"short_text","unique":false,"minLength":0,"maxLength":200},{"id":"blk_software03","ref":"environment","title":"Where is it happening?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_live_for_real","label":"Live, for real users","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_staging_or_test","label":"Staging or test","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_my_own_device","label":"My own device only","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_not_sure","label":"Not sure","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_software04","ref":"started_at","title":"When did it start, as best you know?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"date","disablePast":false,"dateFormat":"YYYY-MM-DD","includeTime":true,"timeStepMinutes":15,"timeMin":"00:00","timeMax":"23:45"},{"id":"blk_software05","ref":"severity","title":"How bad is it right now?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","optio